  it for exact-environment checks and timing.
- **Throughput trick:** on our own GPU VM, run many tasks concurrently against one vLLM server.
  This is the main way to stretch $150.

## Claude usage (Pro plan)
Delegate substantial implementation to `bin/codex-build` with a precise spec and acceptance tests,
then review the result yourself. Use subagents (`.claude/agents/`) sparingly. Don't re-read
unchanged large files. If a cycle is getting long, checkpoint and end with `CONTINUE`.

## Levers, roughly by expected value (re-rank from data)
1. A budget-safe baseline that always yields a non-empty source diff, never edits tests and keeps
